 The thing that sticks out most in my mind about this place was how friendly the staff was. The bartender was so incredibly nice, and he remembered me and what I drank when I would come back for another. It always feels good to know you're treated like you're at home at a bar!"},{"business_id":"Ge9amPrOICifI-dVbaZmEQ","review_id":"VE02-Xwg6NvTs8k2TgBXkA","date":"2013-08-14T15:31:13","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9188746809959412,"text_excerpt":"I enjoyed dining at Tom Foolery's. The staff was very friendly. We asked for a rather complicated cocktail and when it went awry, they offered us a different cocktail at no cost. I didn't fall in love with their chicken batter, but the fries and burger were pretty awesome. In this city it is hard to find a place that doesn't charge inflated tourist prices, but most of the food here is very affordable. The relaxing atmostphere is refershing. Besides that they have televisions and a dart board, and your typical stock of beer and liquors. I would likely eat here again."},{"business_id":"Ge9amPrOICifI-dVbaZmEQ","review_id":"NAdzIy69XL6UFuigA2SEfw","date":"2015-02-11T06:59:42","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8898280262947083,"text_excerpt":"So early in the day we walked by and they had samples of this Cajun pulled pork. It was so delicious & spicy. The flavors lingered in my mouth for hours. So I came back for dinner. Which was great cause the place was dead. So we got immediate service. The silence was so nice. It's right across from the french market. So during the day it's kinda loud & busy. So I ordered the Cajun pulled pork sandwich which came with collard greens, they were so good too. I would definitely recommend this place & come back"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"Ge9amPrOICifI-dVbaZmEQ","photo_id":"4SsZjJ3iUYW_eHxc-iP3yg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/4SsZjJ3iUYW_eHxc-iP3yg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9999999403953552}]},"notebook_case":null}
